{"id":"B17","lessons":[{"id":"B17-L1","recap":[{"back_html":"One that fails when the code is wrong. Break the code once to prove it.","front_html":"A test worth writing"},{"back_html":"Empty input, missing values, zero denominators, one row, duplicate keys.","front_html":"Edge cases for data code"},{"back_html":"pd.testing.assert_frame_equal: values, dtypes, columns and index.","front_html":"Compare DataFrames in tests"},{"back_html":"pytest.approx(expected).","front_html":"Compare floats in tests"}],"snippets":[["<span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">pytest</span>","","","<span class=\"k\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">test_share_zero_total_is_none</span><span class=\"p\">():</span>","    <span class=\"k\">assert</span> <span class=\"n\">share</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">)</span> <span class=\"ow\">is</span> <span class=\"kc\">None</span>","","","<span class=\"nd\">@pytest</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mark</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">parametrize</span><span class=\"p\">((</span><span class=\"s2\">\"part\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"total\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"expected\"</span><span class=\"p\">),</span> <span class=\"p\">[(</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"mi\">4</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"mf\">0.25</span><span class=\"p\">),</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"mf\">0.0</span><span class=\"p\">),</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"mf\">1.0</span><span class=\"p\">)])</span>","<span class=\"k\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">test_share_values</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">part</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">total</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">expected</span><span class=\"p\">):</span>","    <span class=\"k\">assert</span> <span class=\"n\">share</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">part</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">total</span><span class=\"p\">)</span> <span class=\"o\">==</span> <span class=\"n\">expected</span>"]],"takeaway_html":"Test edges on purpose, with tiny explicit inputs, one behaviour per test, and prove each test can fail.","title":"Unit tests for data code that catch real bugs"},{"id":"B17-L2","recap":[{"back_html":"A rule checked against many generated inputs, with failing inputs shrunk to a minimal case.","front_html":"Property-based test"},{"back_html":"Bounds, invariance, round trip, idempotence, grain, and agreement with a slow version.","front_html":"Four data-code properties"},{"back_html":"Includes nan and infinities. Bound it or pass allow_nan=False on purpose.","front_html":"st.floats() default"},{"back_html":".hypothesis/ replays past failures. Keep it out of Git.","front_html":"Hypothesis example database"}],"snippets":[["<span class=\"kn\">from</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">hypothesis</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">import</span> <span class=\"n\">given</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">strategies</span> <span class=\"k\">as</span> <span class=\"n\">st</span>","","<span class=\"nd\">@given</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">st</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">lists</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">st</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">tuples</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">st</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">floats</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"mf\">1e6</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"mf\">1e6</span><span class=\"p\">),</span> <span class=\"n\">st</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">floats</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"mi\">10</span><span class=\"p\">)),</span> <span class=\"n\">min_size</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">))</span>","<span class=\"k\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">test_weighted_mean_within_range</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">pairs</span><span class=\"p\">):</span>","    <span class=\"n\">values</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">v</span> <span class=\"k\">for</span> <span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">_</span> <span class=\"ow\">in</span> <span class=\"n\">pairs</span><span class=\"p\">]</span>","    <span class=\"n\">weights</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">w</span> <span class=\"k\">for</span> <span class=\"n\">_</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">w</span> <span class=\"ow\">in</span> <span class=\"n\">pairs</span><span class=\"p\">]</span>","    <span class=\"n\">m</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">weighted_mean</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">values</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">weights</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>","    <span class=\"k\">assert</span> <span class=\"n\">m</span> <span class=\"ow\">is</span> <span class=\"kc\">None</span> <span class=\"ow\">or</span> <span class=\"nb\">min</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">values</span><span class=\"p\">)</span> <span class=\"o\">-</span> <span class=\"mf\">1e-6</span> <span class=\"o\">&lt;=</span> <span class=\"n\">m</span> <span class=\"o\">&lt;=</span> <span class=\"nb\">max</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">values</span><span class=\"p\">)</span> <span class=\"o\">+</span> <span class=\"mf\">1e-6</span>"]],"takeaway_html":"State a rule that must always hold, generate inputs from the domain the function promises, and let Hypothesis find and shrink the counterexample.","title":"Property-based tests with Hypothesis"},{"id":"B17-L3","recap":[{"back_html":"cProfile with pstats sorted by cumulative, or %prun in a notebook.","front_html":"Find where time goes"},{"back_html":"timeit.repeat or perf_counter. Report the minimum per call.","front_html":"Time a small change"},{"back_html":"tracemalloc peak, and df.memory_usage(deep=True) for pandas.","front_html":"Measure memory"},{"back_html":"Profile, fix the biggest cost, re-measure, keep a test around the change.","front_html":"The order of work"}],"snippets":[["<span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">cProfile</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">pstats</span>","<span class=\"n\">cProfile</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">run</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">\"main()\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"profile.out\"</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>","<span class=\"n\">pstats</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Stats</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">\"profile.out\"</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">sort_stats</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">\"cumulative\"</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">print_stats</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">10</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>"]],"takeaway_html":"Profile to find the cost, time the change with perf_counter or timeit, keep setup out of the timing, and fix the biggest cost first.","title":"Measure before you optimise"}],"pdf":"downloads/cheatsheets/cheatsheet-B17.pdf","summary":"Unit tests, Hypothesis, profiling and memory use.","title":"Testing and performance"}
